  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Four actually inspected2018/2019 whole-side,low entrance,carved facade detail and upper clock-tower pictures,plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM only.No bespoke plans/surveys.Reference photographs viewed only,not downloaded/redistributed;fine icons and letters simplified geometrically.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_of_Christ_the_Saviour_in_Banja_Luka_(01).jpg",
        "author": "Vasyatka1 (Vasily Kudinov)",
        "date": "2019-08-15",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected northeastern whole side, including lower portion. Alternating pale ochre/pink stone bands,gray base,high shallow curved side gable,large circular rose above ornate arched wooden portal and broad rounded steps. Smaller corner bays have little round roses and tall narrow round-headed windows;gilded shallow dome caps sit over arcaded drums. Tall clock tower stands behind/off to one side;main central dome is broader than satellites. Fine lattice/interlace/mosaic icons simplified as geometric relief,not photographed textures."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_of_Christ_the_Saviour_in_Banja_Luka_(06).jpg",
        "author": "Vasyatka1 (Vasily Kudinov)",
        "date": "2019-08-15",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected northwest lower entrance wing. Low pink/ochre banded porch has dark gray metal hip roof,arched central raised front,one dark recessed central doorway and flanking lighter wood doors,white/gray paired column trims and narrow round windows. Broad shallow curved steps reach the entrance. Clock shaft rises immediately behind the low link to the left. Nearby independent city buildings and temporary shop awning/signage are excluded."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_of_Christ_the_Saviour,_Banja_Luka1.jpg",
        "author": "BalkanPhotos",
        "date": "2018-09-21",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected low-angle close side facade. Alternating yellow/rose stone bands and ornate pale white arched surrounds. Large radial rose has geometric star/petal tracery;lower field has repeating diamond/circular pierced-looking motifs above an arched portal/icon field. Curved cornice and small corner arcades support domed caps. Use sparse geometric star/rib/diamond relief;fine icon faces,text/interlace and exact carving are excluded."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belfry_of_Cathedral_of_Christ_the_Saviour_in_Banja_Luka_(1).jpg",
        "author": "Vasyatka1 (Vasily Kudinov)",
        "date": "2019-08-15",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected upper clock tower. Striped square shaft has paired dark louvered round-headed openings below pale round clocks on two visible faces. Curved projecting cornices and stepped square-to-octagonal crown carry a narrow arcade/slit upper stage with pale paired columns and small dark/gold-toned shallow cap and cross. Exact hidden bell/clock arrangement,open-stage engineering and finishes remain picture estimates."
      }
    ]
  }
